WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.750 --> 00:00:03.360
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:06.250 --> 00:00:07.480
NARRATOR: Sandwich
crackers are one

00:00:07.480 --> 00:00:09.670
of life's little conveniences--

00:00:09.670 --> 00:00:12.940
crispy wafers with peanut butter
or cheese spread between them

00:00:12.940 --> 00:00:15.460
all wrapped up in
a neat package.

00:00:15.460 --> 00:00:17.740
In North America,
factories have been mass

00:00:17.740 --> 00:00:21.220
producing these snacks since the
early part of the 20th century

00:00:21.220 --> 00:00:22.975
to satisfy the need to nibble.

00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:30.815
Sandwich crackers come in
handy for a quick refuel.

00:00:32.060 --> 00:00:35.165
Just unwrap and snack while
continuing on your routine.

00:00:37.460 --> 00:00:40.320
They start with the smaller
ingredients for the dough,

00:00:40.320 --> 00:00:45.110
which include baking soda,
a powdered cheese additive,

00:00:45.110 --> 00:00:48.080
and a kind of phosphate,
which, like the baking soda,

00:00:48.080 --> 00:00:49.085
is a leavening agent.

00:00:50.720 --> 00:00:53.810
Next are enzyme
tablets and the yeast,

00:00:53.810 --> 00:00:55.730
two ingredients that
will later cause

00:00:55.730 --> 00:00:58.655
the dough to ferment to give
the crackers textural strength.

00:01:00.080 --> 00:01:02.480
They add water and
thicken the liquefied

00:01:02.480 --> 00:01:04.190
blend with a little flour.

00:01:04.190 --> 00:01:06.830
This makes it easier to
pump into the next mixer.

00:01:08.660 --> 00:01:11.720
This one is a big
trough full of flour.

00:01:11.720 --> 00:01:13.970
They add ice to chill
it and then pipe

00:01:13.970 --> 00:01:16.520
in the small ingredient blend.

00:01:16.520 --> 00:01:20.090
Cooling the mix with ice
preserves the yeast and enzymes

00:01:20.090 --> 00:01:22.430
to hold off on fermentation.

00:01:22.430 --> 00:01:24.590
If fermentation
happens too soon,

00:01:24.590 --> 00:01:27.020
the dough could turn to mush.

00:01:27.020 --> 00:01:30.290
They lower a lid equipped
with three spiraling blades

00:01:30.290 --> 00:01:33.140
and set the blades in
motion, pumping in more water

00:01:33.140 --> 00:01:35.300
to augment the moisture
from the melting ice

00:01:35.300 --> 00:01:36.635
and small ingredient blend.

00:01:38.580 --> 00:01:42.050
It's now ready for fermentation,
so it's into a warm room

00:01:42.050 --> 00:01:44.225
to activate the yeast
and the enzymes.

00:01:45.500 --> 00:01:47.840
The dough swells
and a worker breaks

00:01:47.840 --> 00:01:49.235
the crust to release gas.

00:01:51.110 --> 00:01:53.630
An automated system
tips the trough of dough

00:01:53.630 --> 00:01:55.730
into a chute that
takes it one floor

00:01:55.730 --> 00:01:57.080
down to the rolling station.

00:01:59.120 --> 00:02:01.910
The chemical changes
caused by fermentation

00:02:01.910 --> 00:02:03.740
have made this
dough less sticky,

00:02:03.740 --> 00:02:06.500
so it can now be rolled
into sheets without adhering

00:02:06.500 --> 00:02:07.460
to the equipment.

00:02:08.960 --> 00:02:11.090
The dough now travels
between rollers

00:02:11.090 --> 00:02:14.240
that flatten it and squeeze
it to a specific thickness.

00:02:15.500 --> 00:02:17.930
The sheets of dough
exit and accumulate.

00:02:19.640 --> 00:02:22.700
When several layers have piled
up, the dough is on the move

00:02:22.700 --> 00:02:24.080
again.

00:02:24.080 --> 00:02:26.420
Several layers at a
time now, it moves

00:02:26.420 --> 00:02:29.120
between a series of rollers,
which compress the dough

00:02:29.120 --> 00:02:30.590
to its final thickness.

00:02:32.090 --> 00:02:34.410
A quick dust with
flour and the dough

00:02:34.410 --> 00:02:36.800
now goes under a rolling
cutter that scores

00:02:36.800 --> 00:02:39.890
it to cracker-size proportions.

00:02:39.890 --> 00:02:42.845
The cutter is also spiked with
pins that puncture the dough.

00:02:44.060 --> 00:02:46.220
The holes give the
crackers a dimpled look,

00:02:46.220 --> 00:02:48.080
and they have a
practical purpose--

00:02:48.080 --> 00:02:51.365
allowing steam to escape during
cooking for a crispier snack.

00:02:54.110 --> 00:02:56.240
A sprinkle of salt
and the cracker dough

00:02:56.240 --> 00:02:57.425
now heads into the oven.

00:02:58.860 --> 00:03:01.340
This oven is more
than 65 yards long

00:03:01.340 --> 00:03:03.770
with several heating zones.

00:03:03.770 --> 00:03:06.740
The hottest is around
700 degrees Fahrenheit.

00:03:09.080 --> 00:03:13.130
A roller breaks them cleanly
along the scorelines.

00:03:13.130 --> 00:03:15.495
A quick spray with
vegetable oil adds flavor.

00:03:18.380 --> 00:03:21.530
The crackers then transfer
from one conveyor to another

00:03:21.530 --> 00:03:22.940
and land in neat stacks.

00:03:24.780 --> 00:03:26.610
They head into an
inspection station

00:03:26.610 --> 00:03:29.100
where workers pick out
any damaged crackers

00:03:29.100 --> 00:03:32.370
and adjust the alignment
of the shingled rows

00:03:32.370 --> 00:03:35.730
so it's a smooth transition as
the crackers move into lanes.

00:03:37.470 --> 00:03:41.160
Down the line, workers pull
off samples to weigh them.

00:03:41.160 --> 00:03:44.130
Then equipment flips the
crackers upright, positioning

00:03:44.130 --> 00:03:45.465
them to enter the filling line.

00:03:47.430 --> 00:03:49.020
The peanut butter
filling is ready

00:03:49.020 --> 00:03:52.035
and kept warm so it's smooth
and creamy enough to pump.

00:03:53.400 --> 00:03:55.260
The top crackers
now head downward

00:03:55.260 --> 00:03:59.100
in a precise
configuration, while below,

00:03:59.100 --> 00:04:02.040
the bottom crackers whiz by
the peanut butter depositor.

00:04:04.110 --> 00:04:05.790
It pumps a dollop
of peanut butter

00:04:05.790 --> 00:04:07.140
onto each bottom cracker.

00:04:13.140 --> 00:04:14.970
The peanut butter-covered
bottom crackers

00:04:14.970 --> 00:04:17.475
now move forward to meet
up with the top crackers.

00:04:20.100 --> 00:04:22.530
And again with perfect
timing, the top

00:04:22.530 --> 00:04:25.560
crackers land on the bottom
ones in exact alignment.

00:04:27.060 --> 00:04:29.760
Equipment separates
them into sets of three

00:04:29.760 --> 00:04:32.190
as they head into packaging.

00:04:32.190 --> 00:04:34.920
Plastic wrap envelops
them, and a heat sealer

00:04:34.920 --> 00:04:36.285
cuts and closes the packets.

00:04:40.080 --> 00:04:42.000
Suctioning arms
collect the packets

00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:44.010
and transfer them
to cardboard boxes.

00:04:46.140 --> 00:04:49.680
From mixing to packaging,
it has taken about 24 hours

00:04:49.680 --> 00:04:51.660
to produce a packet
of sandwich crackers.

00:04:53.100 --> 00:04:54.930
Once it reaches
a hungry snacker,

00:04:54.930 --> 00:04:57.000
it will be gone
in no time at all.

00:04:57.000 --> 00:05:00.350
[MUSIC PLAYING]

